  "mn57:8.8": "",
  "mn57:8.9": "This refrain does not appear in the parallel passage in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.233'>AN 4:233</a>. Notice that it also does not appear here in the discussion of kamma that is neither dark nor bright, with neither dark nor bright result. That’s because that kamma does not lead to rebirth.",
  "mn57:8.10": "",
  "mn57:9.1": "",
  "mn57:9.2": "",
  "mn57:9.3": "",
  "mn57:9.4": "",
  "mn57:9.5": "A level of Brahmās who have mastered the third jhāna or the practice of immeasurable empathetic joy. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.123'>AN 4:123</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.125'>AN 4:125</a>.",
  "mn57:9.6": "",
  "mn57:9.7": "",
