  "mn57:10.10": "",
  "mn57:11.1": "",
  "mn57:11.2": "The intention to abandon all forms of kamma—which, because intention is a form of kamma, would have to be abandoned, too—ends the present intentions that go into fabricating the present moment from the raw material provided by past kamma. That total abandoning of present kamma is what provides the opening to the deathless. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn1.1'>SN 1:1</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn22.79'>SN 22:79</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an3.61'>AN 3:62</a>.",
